														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1547688">
									

<p>No, no, I understood that it was supposed to be a field report, but the tonal shift is <em>really</em> startling. The whole beginning of the field report is very terse and impersonal:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Grain silo found at indicated location. Area surrounding silo is a farm in extreme disrepair, no inhabitants. When activated, the entire cone of matter displaced by SCP-1188 is visible in the air in the exact center of this silo.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>…but then you get the last sentence of each paragraph, and they stick out like sore thumbs.</p>
<p>And, while I understand that these are agents making field reports, they're still expected to do so with a certain level of formality. I'm sure that they oft skimp on this expectation, but this feels excessive, at least in contrast to the rest of what was reported.</p>

							</div>

								
					
